Package: tengine
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, adduser, logrotate
Provides: httpd
Description: Tengine HTTP and reverse proxy server
 Tengine is a web server originated by Taobao. It is based on the nginx HTTP
 server and adds many advanced features such as dynamic module loading,
 upstream health checks, session sticky load balancing, request statistics
 and consistent hashing.
 .
 This package ships the server as /usr/sbin/tengine configured through
 /etc/tengine/tengine.conf, which keeps it independent from any nginx
 package installed on the same host.
 .
 It bundles Tongsuo for NTLS and Chinese cryptography, xquic for QUIC and
 HTTP/3, and the LuaJIT based Lua scripting stack. Tongsuo is linked
 statically, so this package does not follow the system OpenSSL and has to be
 rebuilt to pick up TLS security fixes.

Package: tengine-module-perl
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, tengine (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Perl module for Tengine
 ngx_http_perl_module for Tengine, providing the perl, perl_set and
 perl_modules directives.
 .
 The module is dynamic and is NOT loaded automatically. Add
 .
   load_module /usr/lib/tengine/modules/ngx_http_perl_module.so;
 .
 to the main context of /etc/tengine/tengine.conf to enable it.
